From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-aml: mali mpgpu: reject mpgpucmd writes with no argument

mpgpu_write() splits the written string with strsep(&cprt, " "). A write
containing no space leaves cprt NULL, and every command except "preheat"
then uses it unchecked: the mpl2 branch calls strlen(cprt), and the
scmpp, bstgpu, bstpp and lmt branches pass NULL to kstrtouint(), which
reads s[0]. Either way the kernel oopses in the sysfs write path.

The node is 0644, so this needs root, but GPU tuning scripts write it.
On valhall/r44p0 the commands are matched by prefix, so "echo mpl2 >
/sys/class/mpgpu/mpgpucmd" suffices; bifrost/r44p0 compares MAX_TOKEN
(20) bytes and needs echo -n.

Add a branch after the preheat case - the only argument-less command -
that goes to the existing quit label when cprt is NULL. Well-formed
writes are unaffected; a rejected write still returns count, as the
other quit paths do. Only the bifrost/r44p0 and valhall/r44p0 copies
built by package.mk are patched; the other in-tree copies share the bug
but are not compiled. Not exercised on hardware - the pre-patch
reproducer is itself an oops.

--- a/bifrost/r44p0/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mpgpu.c
+++ b/bifrost/r44p0/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mpgpu.c
@@ -81,6 +81,9 @@
 		if (pmali_plat->plat_preheat) {
 			pmali_plat->plat_preheat();
 		}
+	} else if (!cprt) {
+		/* all remaining commands need an argument */
+		goto quit;
 	} else if (!strncmp(pstart, PLL2_CMD, MAX_TOKEN)) {
 		int base = 10;
 		if ((strlen(cprt) > 2) && (cprt[0] == '0') &&
--- a/valhall/r44p0/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mpgpu.c
+++ b/valhall/r44p0/kernel/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/platform/devicetree/mpgpu.c
@@ -80,6 +80,9 @@
 		if (pmali_plat->plat_preheat) {
 			pmali_plat->plat_preheat();
 		}
+	} else if (!cprt) {
+		/* all remaining commands need an argument */
+		goto quit;
 	} else if (!strncmp(pstart, PLL2_CMD, strlen(PLL2_CMD))) {
 		int base = 10;
 		if ((strlen(cprt) > 2) && (cprt[0] == '0') &&
